#
# src/hci/commands/sbenroll_cmd.c adds "sbenroll", which installs the
# platform key hierarchy through EFI_RUNTIME_SERVICES.SetVariable():
# PK first, then KEK (authenticated by PK), then db (authenticated by
# KEK).  The three EFI_VARIABLE_AUTHENTICATION_2 payloads are produced
# at build time by build/sbenroll-gen.py and compiled into the image
# through src/include/ipxe/sbenroll_data.h; no private key is stored in
# the repository or embedded in the image.
#
# The command is idempotent.  When PK, KEK and db already hold the
# generated descriptors nothing is written.  A different PK leaves
# every variable untouched and reports "foreign"; a SetVariable()
# failure reports "failed"; otherwise the result is "ok".  The result
# is published as the "sbenroll-result" setting (DHCP tag 0x66) so a
# control-plane phase script can report it and reboot.
#
# Plain builds keep the stub header and report "failed" without
# touching the variables.  All new files carry
# FILE_LICENCE ( GPL2_OR_LATER_OR_UBDL ); the configuration and header
# edits inherit the upstream licence (GPL-2.0-or-later / UBDL).

